      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. It's a solid draft, but it feels a little... safe? A bit plain. \n\nSince this is for Gastronomy Weekly, we really need the prose to pop and feel more \"high-end.\" The editor mentioned that the descriptive richness score for this draft was a bit on the lower side, so if you could expand on the sensory details—the textures, the smells, the specific way the light hits the wood, the complexity of the flavors—that would be great. \n\nJust remember what I said before though: don't turn it into a list of random adjectives just to hit a number. It needs to flow naturally and stay tasteful. I want the reader to feel like they are actually sitting in the bistro. Can you try a more lush, detailed version?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
